//
// This is the part that is genuinely BILLED. `taxRate()` above is a single global
// rate; a real VAT obligation is per DESTINATION country, with a B2B reverse-charge
// carve-out. The rates below are standard-rate VAT/GST snapshots by ISO-3166 alpha-2
// country. They are conservative inputs to a charge: when we do not recognise a
// country we fall back to the configured `tax_percent` (0 unless the operator set
// one), never to a guess that could overcharge.

/** EU-27 member states — the set the reverse-charge rule applies within. */
